 "schema": 1,
 "_doc": "THE PRINTED LENGTH OF THE CHICAGO POST OFFICE'S 1 JANUARY 1834 RETURN, COUNTED OFF THE PAGE IMAGE (T-0424). Every line of the list as it stands in its ninth and last printing -- Chicago Democrat Vol. I No. 15 of 1834-03-04, page 4, printed column 2 -- read at the scan and set down in printed order, left sub-column first. This is the measurement `tools/letter_list_printings.py` could not make from the transcriptions: the crops it reads carry an interleaved advertisement, so a surname census over them counts the advertisement's words too. `as_printed` is this impression's own setting, verbatim and unamended -- `dane Gray`, `Philip Willaee`, `Joshua Pruvis` stand as the type stands. A `[?]` inside a name is a glyph the image does not carry legibly; a trailing digit is the count of letters waiting, which is how this list marks them.",
